+## fastq-on-idle
+
+The API provides onIdle(): Promise<void> to callback and promise queues. Every call independently resolves once the queue reaches running() === 0 and length() === 0; an already idle queue returns a resolved promise. Waiting must work across pause/resume, multiple concurrent workers, rejection/error completion, kill, killAndDrain and abort of queued work, while waiting for still-running workers. A paused queue with pending tasks is not idle. Do not replace, wrap or overwrite the user-owned drain callback to implement subscription; preserve its identity and ordinary call behavior, including callbacks that enqueue more work. Resolve subscriptions only when the queue is actually idle after those synchronous callbacks. Keep drained() and all existing API behavior compatible.
